<!-- ══════════════════════════════ CH9 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="chapter active" id="ch9">

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">9.1</span>
      <span class="card-title">Capitalized Costs — Historical Cost Principle</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <p>Capitalize the <strong>purchase price + all costs to bring the asset to its intended condition and location.</strong></p>
      <h3>By Asset Type</h3>
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Capitalize</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Land</strong></td><td>Purchase price, closing costs, attorney fees, title insurance, clearing/filling/draining, demolition, assumption of liens</td><td class="warn" style="color:#f0a0aa">Subtract proceeds from salvaged materials!</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Land Improvements</strong></td><td>Fences, parking lots, driveways, landscaping</td><td>Separate depreciable account — limited life</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Buildings</strong></td><td>Materials, labor, overhead, architect fees, permits, excavation, reconditioning</td><td></td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Equipment</strong></td><td>Purchase price, freight & handling, insurance in transit, special foundations, installation, initial testing</td><td></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="rule-box warn"><strong>⚠ Key Point:</strong> Land is NEVER depreciated. Land improvements ARE depreciated (limited life).</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">9.2</span>
      <span class="card-title">Self-Constructed Assets &amp; Interest Capitalization</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <div class="rule-box"><strong>GAAP Rule:</strong> Capitalize actual interest incurred during construction (the lesser of avoidable vs. actual interest).</div>

      <h3>Capitalization Period</h3>
      <p>Begins when ALL three are met: construction starts, expenditures are incurred, AND interest is being incurred.<br>
      Ends when the asset is <em>substantially complete and ready for use</em>, or interest stops.</p>

      <h3>5-Step Calculation</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><p><strong>Weighted-Average Accumulated Expenditures (WAAE)</strong> — Multiply each expenditure × (months remaining ÷ 12).</p></li>
        <li><p><strong>Identify interest rates</strong> — Use specific construction debt rate first (up to that debt's amount), then weighted-average of all other general debt for any excess.</p></li>
        <li><p><strong>Avoidable Interest</strong> = WAAE × appropriate interest rate(s).</p></li>
        <li><p><strong>Actual Interest</strong> = All outstanding principal × stated rates.</p></li>
        <li><p><strong>Capitalize the LESSER</strong> of Avoidable Interest or Actual Interest.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="je">
        <span class="je-label">Journal Entry (Avoidable &lt; Actual)</span>
        <span class="je-dr">Dr. Building ................ [Avoidable Interest]</span>
        <span class="je-dr">Dr. Interest Expense ........ [Actual − Avoidable]</span>
        <span class="je-cr">Cr. Cash .................. [Actual Interest]</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">9.3</span>
      <span class="card-title">Costs Subsequent to Acquisition</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Treatment</th><th>Criteria</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Additions</strong></td><td><em>Capitalize</em></td><td>Always capitalize new additions</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Improvements / Replacements</strong></td><td><em>Capitalize</em></td><td>Extends useful life, increases quantity of output, OR enhances quality of output</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Ordinary Repairs</strong></td><td>Expense</td><td>Routine maintenance — no future benefit</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Major Repairs</strong></td><td><em>Capitalize</em></td><td>Treated as an addition or improvement</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="rule-box">
        <strong>Improvements — Carry Value Known?</strong><br>
        • Old asset's carrying value <em>known</em> → Remove old asset, recognize G/L.<br>
        • Carrying value <em>unknown</em>: Life extended → Dr. Accum. Depr. | Productivity increased → Dr. Asset.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">9.4</span>
      <span class="card-title">Dispositions &amp; Nonmonetary Exchanges</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <div class="rule-box success"><strong>Always first:</strong> Update depreciation to the date of sale or exchange.</div>

      <h3>Commercial Substance?</h3>
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Gain Treatment</th><th>Loss Treatment</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Has Commercial Substance</strong> (cash flows change)</td><td>Recognize immediately</td><td>Recognize immediately</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>No Commercial Substance — no cash</strong></td><td>Defer entire gain; reduce basis of new asset</td><td>Recognize immediately</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>No Commercial Substance — cash/boot received</strong></td><td>Recognize partial gain (see formula)</td><td>Recognize immediately</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Partial Gain Recognition Formula</h3>
      <div class="formula">
        <span class="formula-label">Recognized Gain (No Comm. Substance + Boot Received)</span>
        Recognized Gain = Total Gain × [Cash Received ÷ (Cash Received + FV of Asset Received)]
      </div>
      <div class="rule-box warn"><strong>Exception:</strong> If cash received &gt; 25% of total transaction value → Recognize the ENTIRE gain.</div>
      <p>Asset basis is based on the <strong>Fair Value of asset given up OR received</strong> — use whichever is more clearly evident.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div><!-- /ch9 -->

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ CH10 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="chapter" id="ch10">

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">10.1</span>
      <span class="card-title">Depreciation Concepts &amp; Methods</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <div class="rule-box"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> Depreciation = cost allocation, NOT valuation. It matches expense to periods benefiting from the asset.</div>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="formula-label">Depreciable Base</span>
        Depreciable Base = Cost − Salvage Value
      </div>

      <p><strong>Partial Period:</strong> Calculate to the nearest full month (e.g., bought May 31 → use 7/12 of the year).</p>

      <h3>Depreciation Methods</h3>
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Formula</th><th>Key Rules</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Straight-Line (SL)</strong></td>
              <td><code>(Cost − SV) ÷ Life</code></td>
              <td>Even expense each year; simplest method</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Double-Declining Balance (DDB)</strong></td>
              <td><code>(2 ÷ Life) × Beginning Book Value</code></td>
              <td>Do NOT subtract salvage value from base. Stop when BV = SV. Final year = plug figure.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Sum-of-Years'-Digits (SYD)</strong></td>
              <td><code>(Cost − SV) × (Remaining Years ÷ SYD)</code></td>
              <td>SYD for 5-yr life = 5+4+3+2+1 = 15. Year 1 fraction = 5/15.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Units-of-Production</strong></td>
              <td><code>[(Cost − SV) ÷ Total Units] × Units This Period</code></td>
              <td>Expense varies with actual usage/output</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="rule-box warn"><strong>DDB Critical Rule:</strong> Never deduct salvage value when computing the DDB rate — it's applied to raw book value. But stop depreciating once BV hits salvage value!</div>

      <h3>Changes in Estimates (Prospective Treatment)</h3>
      <p>Do <strong>NOT</strong> restate prior years. Going forward:</p>
      <div class="formula">
        <span class="formula-label">Revised Annual Depreciation</span>
        (Remaining Book Value − New Salvage Value) ÷ Remaining Estimated Life
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">10.2</span>
      <span class="card-title">Depletion of Natural Resources</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <p>Used for timber, oil, mining, and similar wasting assets.</p>
      <div class="formula">
        <span class="formula-label">Depletion Base</span>
        Acquisition Costs + Exploration Costs + Intangible Development Costs + Asset Retirement Obligations − Salvage Value
      </div>
      <div class="formula">
        <span class="formula-label">Depletion Rate</span>
        Rate = Depletion Base ÷ Total Estimated Units
      </div>

      <h3>Journal Entries</h3>
      <div class="je">
        <span class="je-label">Extraction</span>
        <span class="je-dr">Dr. Inventory ............... [Units × Rate]</span>
        <span class="je-cr">Cr. Natural Resource Asset (or Accum. Depletion)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="je">
        <span class="je-label">Sale</span>
        <span class="je-dr">Dr. Cost of Goods Sold (Depletion Expense)</span>
        <span class="je-cr">Cr. Inventory</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-card">
    <div class="card-header" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
      <span class="card-num">10.3</span>
      <span class="card-title">Asset Impairments</span>
      <span class="card-toggle">▾</span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body open">
      <p>Occurs when the book value of a depreciable asset is <strong>not recoverable</strong>.</p>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li><p><strong>Recoverability Test:</strong> Is Book Value &gt; Sum of Undiscounted Expected Future Cash Flows? If YES → impaired.</p></li>
        <li><p><strong>Calculate Loss:</strong> Impairment Loss = Book Value − Fair Value</p></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="je">
        <span class="je-label">Impairment Journal Entry</span>
        <span class="je-dr">Dr. Loss on Impairment ........ [BV − FV]</span>
        <span class="je-cr">Cr. Accumulated Depreciation .. [BV − FV]</span>
      </div>

      <div class="rule-box warn"><strong>Important:</strong> Impairment losses on PP&E generally cannot be reversed under U.S. GAAP once recorded.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div><!-- /ch10 -->

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ CH11 ══════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="chapter" id="ch11">

